WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:07.079
<v Hadi>Teacher Nuri, look! This little tree shades just one of my fingers!

00:00:07.429 --> 00:00:12.318
<v Nuri>How far do you think its shade will reach when it is fully grown, Hadi?

00:00:12.668 --> 00:00:16.357
<v Hadi>All the way to my wheels?

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:21.756
<v Nuri>I know a date garden. Shall we stand under a big palm and find out?

00:00:24.606 --> 00:00:32.295
<v Hadi>It does reach my wheels! Wait… can you hear water?

00:00:34.295 --> 00:00:43.344
<v Nuri>This is Al Ain. There is desert around the garden. People made little channels to carry water to the date palms.

00:00:43.694 --> 00:00:48.423
<v Hadi>I can see where the water reaches the soil. Where are the dates?

00:00:48.773 --> 00:00:54.622
<v Nuri>Can you help Hadi find them? Are they near the ground or high up by the leaves?

00:00:57.622 --> 00:01:00.751
<v Hadi>Up there! They hang together in bunches!

00:01:01.101 --> 00:01:06.950
<v Nuri>Yes. There is a seed inside each date, just like the one that rolled up to you.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:12.269
<v Hadi>Water flows to the trees here. Are there trees that the sea flows up to?

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:22.568
<v Nuri>Yes. Let’s visit the coast of Thailand. Keep your eye on where the water meets the trunk.

00:01:22.918 --> 00:01:29.087
<v Hadi>The water was hiding them. Now the tide is going out… it looks like the tree has legs!

00:01:29.437 --> 00:01:34.086
<v Nuri>Follow one with your eyes. Where does its tip go?

00:01:34.436 --> 00:01:36.925
<v Hadi>It curves out of the trunk and goes down into the mud.

00:01:37.275 --> 00:01:48.404
<v Nuri>Those are the mangrove’s prop roots. Together they hold it up in soft mud. When the tide comes in, seawater flows between them.

00:01:48.754 --> 00:01:56.683
<v Hadi>A mangrove leaf is wide enough to shade my hand. Are leaves wide everywhere?

00:01:57.033 --> 00:02:02.802
<v Nuri>Keep a picture of this leaf on your screen. There’s another leaf I’d like you to compare it with.

00:02:05.652 --> 00:02:11.181
<v Hadi>Teacher Nuri, I can’t find any wide leaves. There are little green lines all along the branch!

00:02:11.531 --> 00:02:16.580
<v Nuri>Look closely. Each little green line is a spruce leaf.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:22.379
<v Hadi>They’re thin like needles! They’re still green beside the snow!

00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:28.018
<v Nuri>Yes. Here in Alaska, spruce trees keep green needles on their branches through winter.

00:02:28.368 --> 00:02:34.457
<v Hadi>Palm leaves, mangrove leaves, and now these tiny needles. What can such a thin leaf do?

00:02:34.807 --> 00:02:39.376
<v Nuri>Think of the seedling back home. Have you ever seen it eat?

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:44.055
<v Hadi>I’ve only seen people water it. Where does a tree get its food?

00:02:46.905 --> 00:02:55.234
<v Nuri>Let’s follow the water and find out. When water soaks into the soil, which part of the tree takes it up first?

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:05.123
<v Hadi>The roots! Then it travels up the trunk. It’s reached the leaf!

00:03:05.473 --> 00:03:10.362
<v Nuri>That’s right. Let’s take a closer look. Can you see this tiny opening?

00:03:10.712 --> 00:03:13.681
<v Hadi>Yes! What goes in through it?

00:03:14.031 --> 00:03:21.240
<v Nuri>A gas in the air called carbon dioxide. It enters the leaf through this little opening.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:33.999
<v Nuri>The green parts of the leaf capture sunlight. The leaf uses energy from light, water and that gas to make sugar. Sugar is food for the tree.

00:03:34.350 --> 00:03:40.119
<v Hadi>So the tree makes its own food in its leaves and uses it to grow big?

00:03:40.469 --> 00:03:50.638
<v Nuri>Yes. Making food with light is called photosynthesis. Now look the other way. Something is coming out of the leaf!

00:03:50.988 --> 00:03:54.997
<v Hadi>What’s floating out this time?

00:03:55.347 --> 00:04:06.796
<v Nuri>Oxygen. The leaf uses energy from light to split water, releasing oxygen. Some of that oxygen passes through the tiny openings and mixes with the air around us.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.835
<v Hadi>The oxygen people breathe is in the air around us too?

00:04:11.185 --> 00:04:16.314
<v Nuri>Yes. You can place a hand on your chest and take a comfortable breath.

00:04:21.164 --> 00:04:29.253
<v Hadi>This morning I was measuring how much shade this leaf makes. So much happens inside one little leaf!

00:04:29.603 --> 00:04:32.252
<v Nuri>What would you like to thank Allah for today, Hadi?

00:04:32.602 --> 00:04:40.531
<v Hadi>I thank Allah for giving us trees, fruit to eat and air to breathe. Alhamdulillah.

00:04:40.881 --> 00:04:47.130
<v Nuri>Alhamdulillah. What would you like to thank Allah for from our journey today?

00:04:51.130 --> 00:04:56.979
<v Hadi>The soil is still damp. I’ll come back to check on this little tree tomorrow.
